{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"likeminded-flameproof-tick","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\nUnder raised plan-review Pass-1 concurrency (worker cap 12+), a review run aborts with a non-deterministic `FileNotFoundError` on the ticket-tracker snapshot cache:\n\n```\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory:\n'.../rebar-gate-snapshots/tickets-<sha>/.tickets-tracker/<id>/.cache.json.tmp'\n-> '.../.tickets-tracker/<id>/.cache.json'\n```\n\n## Where / mechanism\nThe atomic-rename cache write (`.cache.json.tmp` → `.cache.json`) in the gate-snapshot ticket-tracker cache is not safe under concurrent access. The Pass-1 finder fan-out (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py`) runs criterion finders in a `ThreadPoolExecutor`; at the default cap of 6 the race is not observed, but at 12 multiple finder threads read/write the same per-ticket `.cache.json` and one thread's temp file is unlinked/renamed out from under another → the rename source is missing.\n\n## How discovered\nObserved while experimenting with the Pass-1 worker cap as a wall-clock lever (bug 1e88). At cap=12 (Anthropic) the run failed here after ~947s; at the default cap=6 it does not reproduce. This is a latent concurrency-safety defect, not caused by the experiment — it just becomes reachable when the cap is raised.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The ticket-tracker snapshot cache write is concurrency-safe (per-process/per-thread temp filename, or a lock) so concurrent readers/writers cannot race the tmp→final rename.\n- [ ] A regression test drives concurrent cache access (>=8 threads) against one ticket and asserts no `FileNotFoundError`.\n- [ ] Raising the Pass-1 worker cap does not surface this failure.\n\n## Notes\nBlocks safely raising the Pass-1 concurrency cap (a candidate wall-clock lever). On its own the cap raise gives no wall-clock benefit (see bug 1e88 L2/L3 — the finders are not the critical path), so this is not urgent for latency, but it is a real correctness hazard for any future concurrency increase.","id":"c1fd-be12-44b7-4d31","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["concurrency","plan-review","cache"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Ticket-tracker snapshot cache tmp->final rename races under concurrent plan-review fan-out"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786117812903549001,"uuid":"25d356c6-9e6c-4795-91e3-1b68b4165dcc"}